---
title: "From CSS to Zazz"
description: "Every CSS property the utilities write, looked up by the property."
section: Utilities
sectionOrder: 3
order: 13
---

Utilities are named after Tailwind's classes, so `align-items` is `--items` and `border-radius` is `--rounded`. If you know the property and not the class, find it here. Physical names (`width`, `padding-left`) are listed too: the kit writes the logical property, so `--pl` pads the inline start, which is the right side in a right-to-left document.

A value is written the way the property takes it (`--justify: space-between`, `--w: 100%`). Spacing, margin, and sizing utilities also take a bare number as a step on the spacing scale, and a few utilities take a token by name; the [utilities overview](/api/utilities/) has the value rules.

